  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_a18d106853e34f6f8d693e991651dba3",
      "statement": "An error handler is `ErrorHandler = Callable[[Exception], Any]`: it receives only the exception (no DTO, span, layer name or return type) and either returns a value — which suppresses the exception and becomes the bus response verbatim, so a handled failure is indistinguishable from a success at the call site — or re-raises, which the framework treats as a request to delegate to the next handler in the chain.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L60-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4821f07ebffc1659dbe4be2910354f0e05da27aa3151d14a85a13ca903cc76e6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/error_handler.py#L19-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3ed9c7c4dc5ac44aace69fc1b1c772177b2f135023ab2c8011daf5d84ffa72b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/error_handler.py#L3-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fabf14a545a3b15402bd97e3f4adf1344693d56b695eb04b6e1517b0cbddddbe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9933b8d946d9432b9c8eece900966061",
      "statement": "`compose_handler` wraps each handler in `try: return handler(error) except Exception as exc`, so a bug inside a handler is silently converted into the next handler's input exactly like a deliberate delegation, and a handler raising something derived from `BaseException` (KeyboardInterrupt, SystemExit, asyncio.CancelledError) propagates immediately without the remaining handlers running.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/error_handler.py#L33-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aacbee5aebf806ee6efd2372356e91d4b3fceb9ed1056ab4975d26415b0dec57:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_311271ee4d9b4ba597fedd448cd48436",
      "statement": "`build_error_handler_chain` folds the registered list in reverse with `compose_handler`, so the first-registered handler ends up outermost and executes first; it returns `None` for an empty list, which leaves `handle_error` unset and the buses re-raising the original exception.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L60-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4821f07ebffc1659dbe4be2910354f0e05da27aa3151d14a85a13ca903cc76e6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/error_handler.py#L44-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9ed09a224e204939fbc7b85b0b94f0ca85bdbf9624ebdf60387b827bfc8b35a4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d49f11f858354692b58d6bb3b817aec3",
      "statement": "`UseFramework` maintains three independent handler chains — global, feature and app service — and pushes each onto a different bus attribute: `FrameworkBus.handle_error`, `FeatureBus.handle_error` and `ApplicationServiceBus.handle_error`. Each bus holds one optional callable consulted from inside its own `except` block, and the scopes are never merged or nested into one another.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L146-L146",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b6f17d7150481c5b17847ddd27af57332d65c3fcb318bdc8ccbef2b40eae8a6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L26-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b6f17d7150481c5b17847ddd27af57332d65c3fcb318bdc8ccbef2b40eae8a6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L78-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b6f17d7150481c5b17847ddd27af57332d65c3fcb318bdc8ccbef2b40eae8a6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/use_bus.py#L187-L238",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f791b3afe70ea10fc130072d3cb5231c4ec4bf8eb64cafc849ff3a8b468bedab:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6444c4dfd4654ab099e8411979722629",
      "statement": "Which scope sees an exception is decided purely by which bus's `except` clause catches it: a middleware exception is raised before the facade and reaches no handler; a feature handler that returns a value removes the exception before the facade's `except` can see it, so the global handler never runs; an app-service handler sees only what the feature layer re-raised; and the facade handles the sub-bus re-raises plus its own routing errors (`UnknownDTOToExecute`, call-time `DTOAlreadyRegistered`).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L116-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d3f9bd5d6ed2cb14f04ee3393dc7a8806849699d2cad18337bd5a9bfc9f0577:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L174-L205",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:909a42e7b68937c75adc9ba679fca491cfa56a61f587fba67bb910d425bc0419:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L60-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4821f07ebffc1659dbe4be2910354f0e05da27aa3151d14a85a13ca903cc76e6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/middleware.py#L34-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c01d35342a5c07b27b05bc1bcac1ca30a3d1d6316874819e207dc752474894a8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d3a5372fa4354f548ffff4137f04a739",
      "statement": "Nothing above `FrameworkBus.execute` catches anything: `UseFramework.__call__` has no `except` (only a `finally` that pops the implicit overlay), so a middleware exception, `SincproFrameworkNotBuilt`, and anything the facade re-raises reach the caller with no handler consulted and no conversion.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/middleware.py#L45-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b5ac61de90f56a5d96b6675bf36c07d6d3f8e08f9c6a52a691696adaea25b5a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/use_bus.py#L373-L404",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f5f6d43b4f2fea57d4f246ca223c69848898f5f62f58d78a3be05833cae29678:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2bd15e58341b42feb9efcc3b6ae95ec0",
      "statement": "Handlers registered before the build are attached to the container providers: `_add_error_handlers_provided_by_user()` calls `add_attributes(handle_error=…)` on the `framework_bus`, `feature_bus` and `app_service_bus` providers as step 2 of `build_root_bus()`, skipping any scope with no handler so that bus keeps the `None` its `__init__` set.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/use_bus.py#L107-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c6f9c32ab1b64e6c55a10d2c2c788111084df9180108748969b3ec0c3e74095c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1f862d04c2084c188d7a99affc23dbe0",
      "statement": "Handlers registered after the build are assigned straight onto the live bus instances (`self.bus.handle_error`, `self.bus.feature_bus.handle_error`, `self.bus.app_service_bus.handle_error`) behind an `if self.was_initialized and self.bus is not None` guard, and because the composed callable is re-read from the attribute on every `execute` this late registration takes effect immediately with no propagation step.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L62-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:98717d289ee0d4b1a59a134b4f99a41168565db61f529608f5775d0931f45c0a:"
        },
        {
