    {
      "id": "claim_31c2ce329b0a426ba6a197aae2a8c9a8",
      "statement": "Each bus reports the failure through `observability.record_error` inside its `except` block and only then consults `handle_error`, so a swallowing handler still produces a GlitchTip/Sentry event; the error is also recorded on the layer's span (a no-op without OpenTelemetry), and an exception reached through two layers produces two events distinguished by the `sincpro.layer` tag.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L116-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d3f9bd5d6ed2cb14f04ee3393dc7a8806849699d2cad18337bd5a9bfc9f0577:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L60-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4821f07ebffc1659dbe4be2910354f0e05da27aa3151d14a85a13ca903cc76e6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/observability/api.py#L101-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09785ff41d7d70e19419c0ee9936fac02501b10f646160cb6cb3d5e5ff5bde73:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ecb7f33582da4e16930591bac50398d8",
      "statement": "`UseFramework.ignore_sentry_exceptions(*exc_types)` forwards to `Observability.ignore`, which appends unknown types to a tuple read on every report; the ignore list applies only to `kind=\"instance\"` errors (handlers still run for those types) and never to `kind=\"framework\"` errors, because the ignore check precedes the framework release swap.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/observability/api.py#L89-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:276da5261522f5a7c4169d6f422b56ca4d10e47ad5f90ce5804c4192682ab346:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/observability/errors/record_error.py#L32-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:27cc3fc9880495450e38e4fc0990d65d3f20f550644b7d5dc1fb230e8c7cc7f6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/use_bus.py#L240-L247",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4fc1c42b092dc202de3973f5eef3564c8c2e8790231c0e9a49da1e2c6c3c1517:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_62aca5566e0a4087be594faa7afefb91",
      "statement": "`FrameworkBus.execute` reports with `kind=\"framework\"` only for its own routing errors (`UnknownDTOToExecute`, `DTOAlreadyRegistered`), which switches the release to the framework's own distribution and escapes the ignore list; no span is passed at that level, and when no global handler exists the facade logs with `logger.exception` and re-raises the original exception while with a handler present that log line is skipped.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L196-L205",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee12804e3ebe5fbadecaed4ec37dcd8a2b424e80993e5c25ff8ebd0bec718435:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/observability/errors/record_error.py#L35-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:835f753e1c389efeaf3634c07fe311f46872542aac39c459c32e65752b9f8fea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2b19879daf474967a4752f7d7b40a842",
      "statement": "Because `FeatureBus` and `ApplicationServiceBus` are container `Singleton`s while `FrameworkBus` is a `Factory`, a second `build_root_bus()` produces a new facade over the same sub-buses and registries: a handler already assigned to a sub-bus survives the rebuild, whereas the facade's own chain is re-attached from the provider attributes during the build.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/ioc.py#L49-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76c8d4cbeab0e85a5ed437efa7a28ade6214566a9c6fb4cf51b0346ef1bca235:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/use_bus.py#L123-L130",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47a271010e453e66033cd0f4055110035ee9a4621399dbe5f617cc541f76f19f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0da84687ddfa46a9b7534e29105984e5",
      "statement": "The cross-registry `DTOAlreadyRegistered` check runs twice with different handleability: the constructor's check executes during `build_root_bus()`, outside any bus `try`, so its raise cannot reach a handler, while `FrameworkBus.execute`'s per-call re-check sits inside the facade's `try` and therefore does reach the global handler.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L150-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ed1f435d2c77cc7b7c37cda33e0b7e0f4b5980ab47d30de61a196a671d63b392:"
        },
